cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
title: "inscribed-polytopes: maximum-volume polytopes inscribed in the unit sphere"
abstract: >-
  This work presents an experimental methodology for the study of
  maximum-volume polytopes with n vertices inscribed in the unit sphere.
  Rather than introducing new mathematical results, we use the proposed
  approach to reproduce and verify a collection of existing ones. Working from
  the signed-volume polynomial and the Berman-Hanes local optimality condition,
  a single implementation sweeps every combinatorial type of simplicial
  polytope and reproduces the published record on S^2 for 4 <= n <= 12 and on
  S^3 for n <= 8, with every number labelled by an evidence level derived from
  its own data. We also note a failure mode affecting relaxation-based
  approaches: the signed-volume polynomial attains spurious maxima at
  self-intersecting configurations satisfying the optimality condition exactly.
  In four dimensions the sweep winners for 6 <= n <= 8 are convex hulls of two
  regular polygons in orthogonal planes.
type: software
